<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Buton Island</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Butung</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Buton is an island off the south-eastern peninsula of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulawesi">Sulawesi</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, in the province of Southeast Sulawesi. Its main town, Baubau, was the seat of the Sultanate of Buton, which adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> in the 16th century and controlled sea routes between Makassar and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maluku-islands">Moluccas</a>. The island is known for its asphalt deposits and for the great fortress of Wolio.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/buton-island.jpg" alt="Buton Island" width="320" height="393" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sadalmelik · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Buton_Topography.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
